    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just that everything feels so predetermined. like i'm watching a movie of my life but i'm not even the actor, just a background extra. no matter how much i try to hope for something different, the system just pulls me back in. it's like the machine is designed to keep me running until i'm empty. i don't see how anything changes.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
